Acceptance criteria:
  New Atlas and mission chrome has square corners without a global radius reset.
    Preserve static blur, translucency, fine borders, readable type and artwork.
    Intentional circular nodes, orbit rings and icon controls remain circular.
  The single-row header is 69px on desktop and 60px at 760px and below.
    The decorative calendar fits within it; month/day/weekday remain balanced,
    with a complete accessible local date and theme-aware reading ink.
  Compact abbreviations retain the full accessible date. Existing search,
    navigation, theme and tutorial controls remain reachable without overlap.
    Responsive search opens its existing below-header panel when space is tight.
  Calendar weekend strips, local midnight updates, finite turn, restrained hover,
    native-dialog suspension and authoritative reduced motion remain unchanged.
  Recorded streak stays below the saved blocker in each normal mission's rail,
    and remains available for planned missions; counting/data are unchanged.
  The actual graph fits the recovered visible area below the responsive header.
  Preserve browser records, schemas, journal, progress authority, README/media,
    frozen definitions, dependencies, motion budgets and deployment workflow.
  Use only disposable fictional browser contexts, never the owner's profile.
    Technical checks are not independent aesthetic or physical-device approval.
  Publish only reviewed public-safe changes with verified Zanark attribution.
    Exact CI/deployment and actual hosted bytes/affected behavior must succeed.

